 Implementation agreement, functional response, and biological validation answer different questions. Agreement under matched inputs establishes that a calculation was reproduced for those inputs. A corrective reflex response establishes the behavior of the implemented loop. Resemblance to biological organization motivates the model, but quantitative physiological validation would additionally require appropriate measured targets, sensory conditions, and perturbations. The inverse-mechanics activation targets and engineering acceptance thresholds used here have narrower purposes.
 
-Support conditions are equally important to interpretation. Air motion tests coordination without foot loading; supported ground tests introduce contact while retaining specified assistance. Vertical support, lateral guidance, and attitude restraint each alter the mechanical task. None of the program's recorded results establishes harness-free walking. The current BiW2Lvar+ air stages, historical W2L feedback comparison, newer W2L108 ground result, and CAD hybrid-control result therefore demonstrate complementary capabilities without forming one continuous curriculum completed by a single controller.
